# Project: AI-powered Singapore bus catch assistant (AI Lodge Hackathon)

PROJECT_PLAN.md is the source of truth. Follow it. If something conflicts with 
the plan or is missing, ask before deviating.

## Stack
Python 3.11+, FastAPI, httpx, SQLite (stdlib), openai SDK (gpt-4o-mini), pytest.
Frontend: one static index.html with vanilla JS and Leaflet. No Node, no build step.

## Hard rules
- Python computes probability, leave-by, reroute choice, coordinates, and stop 
  selection. OpenAI only explains the fact sheet. Never let the model produce numbers.
- Never show a bare "you'll make it". Show a point value ("about {p}%"); the range is kept for decisions and shown only in the Step 10 notification, the in-app Leave-now banner and the Location uncertain card.
- On stale or failed data: show unavailable/stale, hide the percentage, no leave-now.
- Reject LLM output that changes the range, changes the action, or contains unsafe 
  advice (run, sprint, jaywalk). Fall back to the template sentence (model path dormant).
- Bus-only. Do not add trains, crowding, fares, accounts, background tracking, 
  or walking navigation.

## Secrets
- Read keys from .env only (LTA_ACCOUNT_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ONEMAP_EMAIL, 
  ONEMAP_PASSWORD). Never hardcode, log, or send them to the browser.
- The frontend calls our own API, never LTA, OneMap, or OpenAI directly.

## Workflow
- Build one step from PROJECT_PLAN.md at a time, then stop.
- Tests use fixtures, never live APIs.
- Keep it hackathon-simple. No extra abstractions or dependencies without asking.